WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.742
The BCG matrix sorts a company's brands by market growth and market share.

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:08.280
Stars, cash cows, question marks and dogs.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.714
Each one needs a different budget.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.200
KitKat is a cash cow:

00:00:12.001 --> 00:00:15.006
a huge share of a mature chocolate market,

00:00:15.056 --> 00:00:16.232
throwing off money.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.777
A new Gen Z lolly range is a question mark:

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:19.770
a growing market,

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.470
but a tiny share.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.204
A fading niche line is a dog.

00:00:24.254 --> 00:00:26.174
So milk the cash cow to fund the stars and best question marks,

00:00:26.224 --> 00:00:29.357
and prune the dogs.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.243
Use it like this:

00:00:31.293 --> 00:00:32.234
place each brand on the grid with evidence,

00:00:32.284 --> 00:00:36.289
then show where the budget should flow.
